ngRateWithMultipleViewports"/> specifies whether the primitive fragment shading rate can: be used when multiple viewports are used. If this value is <see cref="T:VK_FALSE"/>, only a single viewport must: be used, and applications must: not write to the <c>ViewportMaskNV</c> or <c>ViewportIndex</c> built-in when setting <c>PrimitiveShadingRateKHR</c>. It must: be <see cref="T:VK_FALSE"/> if the <see cref="M:shaderOutputViewportIndex"/> feature, the `apiext:VK_EXT_shader_viewport_index_layer` extension, the <see cref="M:geometryShader"/> feature is not supported, or if the <see cref="M:primitiveFragmentShadingRate"/> feature is not supported. * [[limits-layeredShadingRateAttachments]] <see cref="M:layeredShadingRateAttachments"/> specifies whether a shading rate attachment image view can: be created with multiple layers. If this value is <see cref="T:VK_FALSE"/>, when creating an image view with a <see cref="M:usage"/> that includes <see cref="T:VK_IMAGE_USAGE_FRAGMENT_SHADING_RATE_ATTACHMENT_BIT_KHR"/>, <see cref="M:layerCount"/> must: be `1`. It must: be <see cref="T:VK_FALSE"/> if the <see cref="M:multiview"/> feature, the <see cref="M:shaderOutputViewportIndex"/> feature, the `apiext:VK_EXT_shader_viewport_index_layer` extension, the <see cref="M:geometryShader"/> feature is not supported, or if the <see cref="M:attachmentFragmentShadingRate"/> feature is not supported. * [[limits-fragmentShadingRateNonTrivialCombinerOps]] <see cref="M:fragmentShadingRateNonTrivialCombinerOps"/> specifies whether <see cref="T:VkFragmentShadingRateCombinerOpKHR"/> enums other than <see cref="T:VK_FRAGMENT_SHADING_RATE_COMBINER_OP_KEEP_KHR"/> or <see cref="T:VK_FRAGMENT_SHADING_RATE_COMBINER_OP_REPLACE_KHR"/> can: be used. It must: be <see cref="T:VK_FALSE"/> unless either the <see cref="M:primitiveFragmentShadingRate"/> or <see cref="M:attachmentFragmentShadingRate"/> feature is supported. * [[limits-maxFragmentSize]] <see cref="M:maxFragmentSize"/> indicates the maximum supported width and height of a fragment. Its <see cref="M:width"/> and <see cref="M:height"/> members must: both be power-of-two values. This limit is purely informational, and is not validated. * [[limits-maxFragmentSizeAspectRatio]] <see cref="M:maxFragmentSizeAspectRatio"/> indicates the maximum ratio between the width and height of a fragment. <see cref="M:maxFragmentSizeAspectRatio"/> must: be a power-of-two value, and must: be less than or equal to the maximum of the <see cref="M:width"/> and <see cref="M:height"/> members of <see cref="M:maxFragmentSize"/>. This limit is purely informational, and is not validated. * [[limits-maxFragmentShadingRateCoverageSamples]] <see cref="M:maxFragmentShadingRateCoverageSamples"/> specifies the maximum number of coverage samples supported in a single fragment. <see cref="M:maxFragmentShadingRateCoverageSamples"/> must: be less than or equal to the product of the <see cref="M:width"/> and <see cref="M:height"/> members of <see cref="M:maxFragmentSize"/>, and the sample count reported by <see cref="M:maxFragmentShadingRateRasterizationSamples"/>. <see cref="M:maxFragmentShadingRateCoverageSamples"/> must: be less than or equal to [eq]#<see cref="M:maxSampleMaskWords"/> {times} 32# if <see cref="M:fragmentShadingRateWithShaderSampleMask"/> is supported. This limit is purely informational, and is not validated. * [[limits-maxFragmentShadingRateRasterizationSamples]] <see cref="M:maxFragmentShadingRateRasterizationSamples"/> is a <see cref="T:VkSampleCountFlagBits"/> value specifying the maximum sample rate supported when a fragment covers multiple pixels. This limit is purely informational, and is not validated. * [[limits-fragmentShadingRateWithShaderDepthStencilWrites]] <see cref="M:fragmentShadingRateWithShaderDepthStencilWrites"/> specifies whether the implementation supports writing <c>FragDepth</c> or <c>FragStencilRefEXT</c> from a fragment shader for multi-pixel fragments. If this value is <see cref="T:VK_FALSE"/>, writing to those built-ins will clamp the fragment shading rate to [eq]#(1,1)#. * [[limits-fragmentShadingRateWithSampleMask]] <see cref="M:fragmentShadingRateWithSampleMask"/> specifies whether the implementation supports setting valid bits of <see cref="T:VkPipelineMultisampleStateCreateInfo.pSampleMask"/> to `0` for multi-pixel fragments. If this value is <see cref="T:VK_FALSE"/>, zeroing valid bits in the sample mask will clamp the fragment shading rate to [eq]#(1,1)#. * [[limits-fragmentShadingRateWithShaderSampleMask]] <see cref="M:fragmentShadingRateWithShaderSampleMask"/> specifies whether the implementation supports reading or writing <c>SampleMask</c> for multi-pixel fragments. If this value is <see cref="T:VK_FALSE"/>, using that built-in will clamp the fragment shading rate to [eq]#(1,1)#. * [[limits-fragmentShadingRateWithConservativeRasterization]] <see cref="M:fragmentShadingRateWithConservativeRasterization"/> ifndef::VK_EXT_conservative_rasterization[] is reserved for future use. specifies whether conservative rasterization is supported for multi-pixel fragments. It must: be <see cref="T:VK_FALSE"/> if `apiext:VK_EXT_conservative_rasterization` is not supported. If this value is <see cref="T:VK_FALSE"/>, using conservative rasterization will clamp the fragment shading rate to [eq]#(1,1)#. * [[limits-fragmentShadingRateWithFragmentShaderInterlock]] <see cref="M:fragmentShadingRateWithFragmentShaderInterlock"/> ifndef::VK_EXT_fragment_shader_interlock[] is reserved for future use. specifies whether fragment shader interlock is supported for multi-pixel fragments. It must: be <see cref="T:VK_FALSE"/> if `apiext:VK_EXT_fragment_shader_interlock` is not supported. If this value is <see cref="T:VK_FALSE"/>, using fragment shader interlock will clamp the fragment shading rate to [eq]#(1,1)#. * [[limits-fragmentShadingRateWithCustomSampleLocations]] <see cref="M:fragmentShadingRateWithCustomSampleLocations"/> ifndef::VK_EXT_sample_locations[] is reserved for future use. specifies whether custom sample locations are supported for multi-pixel fragments. It must: be <see cref="T:VK_FALSE"/> if `apiext:VK_EXT_sample_locations` is not supported. If this value is <see cref="T:VK_FALSE"/>, using custom sample locations will clamp the fragment shading rate to [eq]#(1,1)#. * [[limits-fragmentShadingRateStrictMultiplyCombiner]] <see cref="M:fragmentShadingRateStrictMultiplyCombiner"/> specifies whether <see cref="T:VK_FRAGMENT_SHADING_RATE_COMBINER_OP_MUL_KHR"/> accurately performs a multiplication or not. Implementations where this value is <see cref="T:VK_FALSE"/> will instead combine rates with an addition. If <see cref="M:fragmentShadingRateNonTrivialCombinerOps"/> is <see cref="T:VK_FALSE"/>, implementations must: report this as <see cref="T:VK_FALSE"/>. If <see cref="M:fragmentShadingRateNonTrivialCombinerOps"/> is <see cref="T:VK_TRUE"/>, implementations should: report this as <see cref="T:VK_TRUE"/>.
            /// </summary>
            public void* pNext;
            
