treamsLinesTriangles"/> is <see cref="T:VK_TRUE"/> if the implementation supports the geometry shader <c>OpExecutionMode</c> of <c>OutputLineStrip</c> and <c>OutputTriangleStrip</c> in addition to <c>OutputPoints</c> when more than one vertex stream is output. If <see cref="M:transformFeedbackStreamsLinesTriangles"/> is <see cref="T:VK_FALSE"/> the implementation only supports an <c>OpExecutionMode</c> of <c>OutputPoints</c> when more than one vertex stream is output from the geometry shader. * [[limits-transformFeedbackRasterizationStreamSelect]] <see cref="M:transformFeedbackRasterizationStreamSelect"/> is <see cref="T:VK_TRUE"/> if the implementation supports the <c>GeometryStreams</c> SPIR-V capability and the application can use <see cref="T:VkPipelineRasterizationStateStreamCreateInfoEXT"/> to modify which vertex stream output is used for rasterization. Otherwise vertex stream `0` must: always be used for rasterization. * [[limits-transformFeedbackDraw]] <see cref="M:transformFeedbackDraw"/> is <see cref="T:VK_TRUE"/> if the implementation supports the <see cref="M:vkCmdDrawIndirectByteCountEXT"/> function otherwise the function must: not be called.
